    "title": "Markets inside the walls",
    "p1": "El Jadida’s souks are working markets more than tourist bazaars: produce, spices, household goods and the daily traffic of the medina.",
    "p2": "Morning is liveliest. Bargain politely where expected, keep bags close, and step aside for carts in narrow lanes.",
    "p3": "Use the souks as the connective tissue between the Portuguese monuments, the Mellah and the port."
